VALUES (gen_random_uuid()::text, $q$talleez-video-tally-game$q$, $q$Talleez: Interactive Video Tally Game$q$, $q$A counting game where players watch video clips and tap to tally things in real time. The client’s idea was built around sports like the NBA and NFL, and concert videos of artists like Ariana Grande and Pharrell Williams. The content keeps getting updated over time.$q$, $q$Casual & Puzzle$q$, ARRAY[$q$Mobile Game$q$, $q$Casual$q$, $q$Interactive Media$q$, $q$Video$q$, $q$Unity$q$]::text[], $q$Unity, C#, Unity UI, VideoPlayer API, REST API, iOS and Android$q$, $q$2024$q$, $q$🎬$q$, $q$#be185d$q$, true, 8, $q$GAME$q$, $q$COMPANY$q$, $q$Solo developer$q$, $q$I built the whole game on my own, from the video tally system and screen orientation handling to the score screens and the server connection. I keep updating it with new content.$q$, ARRAY[$q$Tally buttons that stay in sync with the video as it plays$q$, $q$Automatic switching between portrait menus and landscape video sessions$q$, $q$Animated button feedback and effects so tapping feels satisfying$q$, $q$Score breakdown screens showing accuracy$q$, $q$Server communication for login and score saving$q$, $q$Custom video controls with a progress bar and scrubber$q$]::text[], ARRAY[$q$Solo, with the client directing the concept$q$]::text[], NULL, ARRAY[$q$Real time tallying on top of video$q$, $q$Portrait and landscape challenges$q$, $q$Custom video player controls$q$, $q$End of round breakdown with accuracy$q$, $q$Configurable tally targets such as words, icons or numbers$q$]::text[], ARRAY[$q$Runtime orientation and resolution handling per video aspect ratio, with no black bars$q$, $q$Event driven design that keeps UI and gameplay separate$q$, $q$Async networking with UnityWebRequest and cancellation support$q$]::text[], $q$iOS, Android$q$, false, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
