VALUES (gen_random_uuid()::text, $q$duck-race-multiplayer$q$, $q$DuckRace: Multiplayer Duck Racing$q$, $q$A 2D duck racing game with single player and multiplayer races, accounts, and an animated leaderboard. Multiplayer uses a host and client setup where one player hosts the room and others join.$q$, $q$Multiplayer & Sports$q$, ARRAY[$q$2D$q$, $q$Multiplayer$q$, $q$Racing$q$, $q$Unity$q$, $q$Photon Fusion$q$, $q$Firebase$q$, $q$Mobile$q$]::text[], $q$Unity, C#, Photon Fusion, Firebase Authentication, DOTween$q$, $q$2025$q$, $q$🦆$q$, $q$#0284c7$q$, true, 2, $q$GAME$q$, $q$COMPANY$q$, $q$Solo gameplay and multiplayer developer$q$, $q$I built the whole game myself: race gameplay, sign in, lobby, rooms and results. I also tried setting up a Hetzner VPS with server control and load balancing, but I was not experienced enough at that point to finish it.$q$, ARRAY[$q$Single player racing with random duck speed, finish detection and a following camera$q$, $q$Email sign up and login with Firebase$q$, $q$Multiplayer lobby, public and private rooms and networked duck spawning$q$, $q$Synchronized race start and finish$q$, $q$Late join spectating$q$, $q$Bot takeover when a player disconnects$q$, $q$Animated leaderboard with DOTween$q$]::text[], ARRAY[$q$Solo$q$]::text[], NULL, ARRAY[$q$Account registration and login$q$, $q$Single player and multiplayer races$q$, $q$Up to 16 players in a session$q$, $q$Spectator state for people joining mid race$q$, $q$Disconnect handling$q$, $q$Animated results and winner highlight$q$]::text[], ARRAY[$q$Host and client structure with synchronized race state$q$, $q$Late joiners see a “race in progress” state instead of breaking the race$q$, $q$When someone drops, their duck turns into a bot$q$, $q$Attempted Hetzner VPS hosting and load balancing, which taught me a lot about server side limits$q$]::text[], $q$Android and desktop$q$, false, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
