VALUES (gen_random_uuid()::text, $q$react-native-unity-bridge$q$, $q$ReactWithUnity: Unity Inside a React Native App$q$, $q$My first task at my first part time job at EuphoriaXR. My CEO asked me to run a Unity app inside a React Native app. The result is a mobile app where React Native handles the screens and navigation, and Unity loads inside it with messages going both ways.$q$, $q$AR/VR & Tools$q$, ARRAY[$q$Unity$q$, $q$React Native$q$, $q$Mobile$q$, $q$Android$q$, $q$iOS$q$, $q$Integration$q$]::text[], $q$Unity, C#, React Native, TypeScript, Kotlin, Objective-C++, Android, iOS$q$, $q$2025$q$, $q$📱$q$, $q$#0f172a$q$, true, 10, $q$GAME$q$, $q$COMPANY$q$, $q$Mobile and Unity integration developer$q$, $q$I embedded the Unity runtime into a React Native app and set up communication so React Native can start and control a geospatial scene inside Unity and receive messages back.$q$, ARRAY[$q$React Native shell with a home screen and navigation$q$, $q$Embedded Unity screen inside the app$q$, $q$Messages from React Native to Unity to start the scene$q$, $q$Android integration using the generated Unity library$q$, $q$iOS project setup$q$]::text[], ARRAY[$q$EuphoriaXR$q$]::text[], $q$Employee of the Month at EuphoriaXR for this work.$q$, ARRAY[$q$Navigation from the React Native home screen into Unity$q$, $q$Delayed Unity start after the view loads$q$, $q$JSON messages sent to Unity$q$, $q$Messages from Unity logged back in React Native$q$, $q$Support for multiple Android architectures$q$]::text[], ARRAY[$q$Unity Android library added to a React Native project through Gradle$q$, $q$TypeScript to Unity messaging using game object, method name and JSON$q$, $q$Works with Unity IL2CPP output and native libraries$q$]::text[], $q$Android and iOS$q$, false, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
