VALUES (gen_random_uuid()::text, $q$threshold-ai-roguelike$q$, $q$Threshold: Agentic AI Top-Down Shooter$q$, $q$A mobile top down roguelike shooter where AI adapts the difficulty, dungeon layout, enemy tactics and rewards to how each player plays. It combines regular procedural generation with a five agent AI pipeline, and falls back to local logic if AI is not available.$q$, $q$Action & Shooter$q$, ARRAY[$q$Game AI$q$, $q$Adaptive Difficulty$q$, $q$Procedural Generation$q$, $q$Roguelike$q$, $q$Shooter$q$, $q$Mobile$q$, $q$LLM$q$]::text[], $q$Unity 6, C#, Unity AI Navigation, URP, Input System, Gemini, Groq, NVIDIA NIM$q$, $q$2026$q$, $q$🤖$q$, $q$#1b1035$q$, true, 1, $q$GAME$q$, $q$HACKATHON$q$, $q$Developer$q$, $q$I worked on the dungeon generation, the AI pipeline, enemy behaviour, the core gameplay loop and progression, with a second developer and a UI/UX designer.$q$, ARRAY[$q$Hybrid dungeon generation: local code builds the room layout and checks it is reachable, while AI decides what each room is for$q$, $q$Five agents: director, level generation, quality control, NPC brain and rewards$q$, $q$One bridge that works with Gemini, Groq and NVIDIA NIM, with retries and rate limit handling$q$, $q$Four enemy types with a tactical state machine for patrol, attack, flank, suppress and retreat$q$, $q$Defection system where badly wounded enemies can switch sides$q$, $q$Twin stick mobile controls, shooting, reload, health and pickups$q$, $q$XP, personalized challenges and cheat checks$q$, $q$A comparison mode between the adaptive AI and fixed rules$q$]::text[], ARRAY[$q$Me$q$, $q$One more developer$q$, $q$One UI/UX designer$q$]::text[], $q$5th place regionally at Google AI Seekho 2026.$q$, ARRAY[$q$Procedurally generated floors$q$, $q$AI adjusted difficulty$q$, $q$Four enemy archetypes$q$, $q$Enemies that flank, suppress and switch sides$q$, $q$Boss, ambush and loot rooms$q$, $q$Works offline with local fallbacks$q$, $q$Mock AI mode for testing without API costs$q$]::text[], ARRAY[$q$Spatial layout stays in local code, AI only assigns roles, so layouts are always valid$q$, $q$Layout checks for reachability and matching doorways, with automatic repair$q$, $q$Every AI response carries a reasoning trace that can be exported for debugging$q$, $q$The game never stops if AI fails, it falls back to a playable local state$q$]::text[], $q$Android, with editor and PC for testing$q$, false, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
